      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your grandma is wrong; butter traps heat and acts like a tourniquet, making the burn worse, while tea tree oil is too potent and will cause a chemical burn on open skin. You must apply plain, cool water immediately to stop the \"cooking\" process, and only use sterile saline or plain water for cleaning the blistered area. Do not apply anything else until the skin has cooled down completely, or you risk permanent scarring and infection.",
